I will not abuse being a member of this group, and intend to listen much
more than speak. However, I have something that I think you will all respect
(may not agree with). This is a philosophical debate between myself and the
freenet community, which is basically a better version of Gnutella. In my
opinion, they hide behind the first amendment a bit too much. They believe
that true distributed security is achievable (I do not, by definition).

Tomorrow I'm having a conference call with VA Linux, to get a quote. The
business plan will be ready in a month. Then funding, then code. I will talk
to all of you after I have achieved these.

